From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alp Lab AB <contact@alplab.ai>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 11:43:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] rzv2n-dev: ALP E1M: persistent environment with a write
 allowlist, no "env default -a" every boot

CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND opened with "env default -a", so every saved variable
was thrown away on every boot and saveenv could never stick.  Drop it.

Persisting the whole environment would let a saved copy (or Linux's
fw_setenv) replace bootcmd, bootargs, bootdelay/bootstopkey* and the
vendor boot scripts bootcmd runs, so the environment is restricted with
CONFIG_ENV_WRITEABLE_LIST: the built-in default is the baseline on every
boot and only the variables in CFG_ENV_FLAGS_LIST_STATIC (the OTA
variables and the alp_envinit marker) are read back from the saved copy.
Everything that controls booting is therefore always rebuilt from this
binary.  The console is unaffected: setenv/saveenv work as before, only
the load filters.

alp_env_check() (board_late_init) only handles the first boot: with no
alp_envinit marker it writes the defaults out once so "bad CRC" is not
printed again.  alp_eth_mac still overwrites ethaddr/eth1addr every boot.

The environment's location (redundant pair in eMMC boot partition 2) and
CONFIG_ENV_WRITEABLE_LIST are set by meta-alp-sdk's uboot-env-emmc.cfg,
not here.

Not verified on silicon.

Signed-off-by: Alp Lab AB <contact@alplab.ai>
---
 board/renesas/rzv2n-dev/rzv2n-dev.c | 48 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 include/configs/rzv2n-dev.h         | 35 ++++++++++++++++++---------
 2 files changed, 65 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

diff --git a/board/renesas/rzv2n-dev/rzv2n-dev.c b/board/renesas/rzv2n-dev/rzv2n-dev.c
index 4ea3287e..1737e870 100644
--- a/board/renesas/rzv2n-dev/rzv2n-dev.c
+++ b/board/renesas/rzv2n-dev/rzv2n-dev.c
@@ -1051,15 +1051,14 @@ static void alp_eth_format_mac(const u8 mac[6], char out[18])
  * a purchased IEEE OUI block).  See scripts/alp_eth_mac.py for the
  * shared golden vector and docs/soms/v2n.md for the policy writeup.
  *
- * Always overwrites -- there is no env override slot on this board:
- * CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND opens with "env default -a", which wipes the
- * whole environment back to its compiled-in defaults before Linux is
- * ever reached, so a saved override could not survive to the next
- * autoboot regardless of what this function did.  This is called both
+ * Always overwrites -- there is no env override slot on this board: the
+ * MAC is re-derived from the unit's identity on every boot, so a saved
+ * ethaddr/eth1addr does not survive to the next autoboot even though the
+ * rest of the environment now persists.  This is called both
  * from board_late_init() (so U-Boot's own networking has a MAC before
  * bootcmd runs) and from the "alp_eth_mac" command CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND
- * (include/configs/rzv2n-dev.h) runs immediately after "env default
- * -a" -- the second call is the one that matters for Linux: boot/
+ * (include/configs/rzv2n-dev.h) runs first -- the second call is the
+ * one that matters for Linux: boot/
  * image-fdt.c's image_setup_libfdt() calls fdt_fixup_ethernet() (which
  * reads ethaddr/eth1addr straight out of env into the ethernet0/
  * ethernet1 DT nodes' mac-address/local-mac-address properties)
@@ -1224,11 +1223,46 @@ static void alp_gd32_nrst_release(void)
 	       ALP_ACT88760_GPIO_REG, before, after);
 }
 
+/*
+ * Persistent environment (eMMC boot partition 2, two copies -- see
+ * meta-alp-sdk's uboot-env-emmc.cfg).  The previous bootcmd opened with
+ * "env default -a" and so threw away every saved variable on every boot.
+ *
+ * CONFIG_ENV_WRITEABLE_LIST (include/configs/rzv2n-dev.h lists the
+ * variables) makes the compiled-in default environment the baseline on
+ * every boot and imports only the listed OTA variables from the saved
+ * copy.  bootcmd, bootargs, bootdelay, the vendor boot scripts and every
+ * other variable are therefore always rebuilt from this binary, whatever
+ * Linux's fw_setenv (or an older U-Boot) wrote.
+ *
+ * What is left for this code is the first boot: both copies unreadable
+ * (blank or never written), U-Boot used the defaults and printed "bad CRC",
+ * so write them out once.  alp_envinit is on the writeable list, so from
+ * then on the saved copy carries it and "Loading Environment" is silent.
+ */
+static void alp_env_check(void)
+{
+	int ret;
+
+	if (env_get("alp_envinit"))
+		return;
+
+	ret = env_set("alp_envinit", "1");
+	if (!ret)
+		ret = env_save();
+	if (ret)
+		printf("ALP: WARNING: environment not saved (%d); it will "
+		       "not persist\n", ret);
+	else
+		printf("ALP: environment initialised\n");
+}
+
 int board_late_init(void)
 {
 	bool v2n_m1;
 	bool rail_ok = true;
 
+	alp_env_check();
 	alp_gd32_nrst_release();
 	alp_clk5l_fixup();
 
diff --git a/include/configs/rzv2n-dev.h b/include/configs/rzv2n-dev.h
index 4ee9d7e5..21d3547e 100644
--- a/include/configs/rzv2n-dev.h
+++ b/include/configs/rzv2n-dev.h
@@ -132,7 +132,7 @@
  * prod-boot.cfg uses).  It is a BUILD-time selection, which is correct
  * while one MACHINE produces one image.  An EEPROM-manifest-derived
  * fdtfile -- one image booting on several SKUs -- remains future work
- * and would have to be set AFTER the leading "env default -a" wipe. */
+ * and would have to be set at CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND, not saved in the env. */
 /* ALP: the dtb basename is a per-SKU Kconfig string, not a literal.
  * V2N SKUs build e1m-v2n101-x-evk.dtb and V2M SKUs build
  * e1m-v2m101-x-evk.dtb (meta-alp-sdk/conf/machine/e1m-v2{n,m}10*-a55.conf,
@@ -160,22 +160,35 @@
  * customer data card) must fall back to the eMMC, not stop at the
  * prompt. */
 /* ALP: alp_eth_mac (patch 0010, board/renesas/rzv2n-dev/rzv2n-dev.c) runs
- * here, immediately after "env default -a" and before anything else --
- * that leading env reset is why the per-unit ethaddr/eth1addr derivation
- * cannot live in board_late_init() alone: board_late_init() runs once,
- * long before bootcmd, so whatever it sets into env is wiped by this
- * same "env default -a" a few tokens later.  Running the derivation
- * again here, post-wipe, is what makes it visible to the booti path's
- * fdt_fixup_ethernet() (boot/image-fdt.c's image_setup_libfdt(), which
- * runs it BEFORE ft_system_setup() -- confirmed by reading this BSP's
- * actual 2024.07 source, not assumed). */
+ * here, before anything else, so the per-unit ethaddr/eth1addr derived
+ * from the unit identity is what the booti path's fdt_fixup_ethernet()
+ * (boot/image-fdt.c's image_setup_libfdt(), which runs it BEFORE
+ * ft_system_setup() -- confirmed by reading this BSP's actual 2024.07
+ * source, not assumed) copies into the DT, whatever a saved environment
+ * holds.  It overwrites unconditionally, so a saved MAC never wins. */
 /* ALP: "alp_sd_present" (patch 0013) reads the microSD card-detect pin.
  * An empty slot goes straight to the vendor eMMC loader, i.e. what
  * bootcmd_check ("if mmc dev 1; then run sd2load; else run emmcload; fi")
  * would end up running, without mmc1 ever being probed: sh_sdhi cannot
  * report card presence, so "mmc dev 1" on an empty slot spends its time
  * failing "Card did not respond to voltage select! : -110". */
-#define CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND	"env default -a;alp_eth_mac;" \
+#ifdef CONFIG_ENV_WRITEABLE_LIST
+/* ALP: the only variables read back from the saved environment ("sw" =
+ * string, writeable): Mender's U-Boot integration (upgrade_available,
+ * bootcount, mender_boot_part, mender_boot_part_hex, mender_saveenv_canary)
+ * and the alp_envinit first-boot marker.  Everything else -- bootcmd,
+ * bootargs, bootdelay, bootstopkey*, preboot, the vendor boot scripts --
+ * is rebuilt from the built-in default on every boot. */
+#define CFG_ENV_FLAGS_LIST_STATIC \
+	"alp_envinit:sw,upgrade_available:sw,bootcount:sw," \
+	"mender_boot_part:sw,mender_boot_part_hex:sw,mender_saveenv_canary:sw"
+#endif
+
+/* ALP: no "env default -a" here any more -- the environment persists in
+ * eMMC boot partition 2, but CONFIG_ENV_WRITEABLE_LIST (above) makes the
+ * compiled-in default the baseline on every boot, so this command and the
+ * vendor scripts it runs can never be replaced by a saved copy. */
+#define CONFIG_BOOTCOMMAND	"alp_eth_mac;" \
 	"if alp_sd_present; then run bootcmd_check; else run emmcload; fi;" \
 	"if alp_sd_present && mmc dev 1 && ext4size mmc 1:2 boot/Image; then " \
 	"setenv alp_mmc 1:2;setenv alp_root /dev/mmcblk1p2; else " \
